1
00:00:01,530 --> 00:00:03,530
== sync, corrected by elderman ==
@elder_man

2
00:00:08,339 --> 00:00:09,969
(Penny:)Well, where is he?

3
00:00:09,974 --> 00:00:11,104
(Amy:)Sheldon?

4
00:00:11,108 --> 00:00:12,138
(Leonard:)I'll check his room.

5
00:00:12,143 --> 00:00:13,473
Surprise!
(both scream)

6
00:00:13,477 --> 00:00:14,607
Oh, my God!

7
00:00:14,612 --> 00:00:16,582
(Sheldon:)Just one example

8
00:00:16,581 --> 00:00:19,181
(Sheldon:)of how birthdays
can be terrible.

9
00:00:19,183 --> 00:00:21,453
(Sheldon:)Now, can we please

10
00:00:21,452 --> 00:00:22,822
(Sheldon:)drop this subject
and pick a new one?

11
00:00:22,820 --> 00:00:25,350
Yeah, I suggest
“how thick can a soup get

12
00:00:25,356 --> 00:00:26,856
before it becomes a stew?”

13
00:00:26,858 --> 00:00:29,288
(Sheldon:)You know, the answer,
it may surprise you.

14
00:00:29,293 --> 00:00:32,163
(Amy:)I'm sorry I brought it up.

15
00:00:32,163 --> 00:00:33,393
(Penny:)Yeah, what is the problem?

16
00:00:33,397 --> 00:00:34,427
(Penny:)Is it about getting older?

17
00:00:34,432 --> 00:00:36,862
(Sheldon:)Please, look at this
porcelain skin.

18
00:00:36,868 --> 00:00:39,668
(Sheldon:)I'm like a human sink.

19
00:00:40,972 --> 00:00:44,872
(Amy:)But it's the one day a year
that's just all about you.

20
00:00:44,876 --> 00:00:46,846
(Amy:)One day.
(laughs)

21
00:00:50,181 --> 00:00:51,451
(Leonard:)Right.

22
00:00:53,384 --> 00:00:55,354
(Amy:)Can you please just tell me why?

23
00:00:55,353 --> 00:00:58,423
(Sheldon:)Fine.

24
00:00:58,422 --> 00:01:00,592
(Sheldon:)As you know,
I have a twin sister

25
00:01:00,591 --> 00:01:03,091
(Sheldon:)with whom I obviously
share a birthday.

